                <pb facs="0249" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v14/pg219"/>

                <head>71. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On August 17, 1960, the Republic of Gabon became independent. For text of a
                    message of that date from President Eisenhower to Prime Minister Leon M’ba, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the Presidents of the United States:
                            Dwight D. Eisenhower,
                        1960–61</hi>, page 644. Consul General at Brazzaville Alan W. Lukens
                    presented his credentials as Chargé d’Affaires on August 17; see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 31, 1960, page 702. Lukens
                    was resident at Brazzaville, as was the first Ambassador to Gabon, W. Wendell
                    Blancké, who presented his credentials on January 13, 1961.</p>
            </div>
